 "section_summary": "This section comprises U.S. Embassy Tokyo's Monthly Political Reports on conditions in Japan for May, June, and July 1937 (Reports No. 128, 129, and 130), transmitted by Ambassador Joseph C. Grew. It details major internal and international developments, including the collapse of the Hayashi Cabinet and installation of Prince Fumimaro Konoe's Cabinet in early June, followed by the outbreak of full-scale hostilities in North China after the Marco Polo Bridge Incident in July. In foreign affairs, the reports cover Japanese rejections of qualitative naval gun caliber limitations, diplomatic exchanges over Alaskan salmon fisheries, armed border clashes with Soviet forces on the Amur River, and initial domestic economic mobilization and exchange controls to finance military operations.",
